`dead_letter.requeue`: the dead letter at trigger sequence 14 (event `00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000001026`) is for a trigger whose run has a start on record: invocation `6c000000-0000-7000-8000-00000000000c`, on its claim, marked durably started. Requeueing it would run the work twice, so nothing was reserved or published, and `checked_not_started` (`--checked-not-started`) does not change that: it is for a run the daemon cannot tell about, never one with a start on record. Read the run with `fq invocation show 6c000000-0000-7000-8000-00000000000c` (`invocation.get`). To run the work again anyway, publish it as new work with `trigger.publish`. Its claim: already marked started.
